{"ts":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"93c1cb9c51cd52f327b34f44","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-2lex4r"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm measure: a named population over the workspace declared as data, with a composable source vocabulary and derived arithmetic so a bound can be denominated in the unit it actually means"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"A measurement is a named, saved, declarative query over the workspace that resolves to a number or a labelled set of numbers. Sources compose: items (a filter expression over status/type/tags/priority/fields/dates), dependency_kind (typed edge counts), graph (any numeric field of any analytic — analyze, redundancy, articulation, centrality, communities, dominators, slack), validate and health (warning and check populations), history (counts over the immutable stream: ops, authors, provenance fields, inter-arrival recurrence), links (linked file/test/doc presence and staleness), and provider (contributed by an extension). The decisive addition is derived: an arithmetic expression over other measurements, evaluated by the SDK. Denomination is the difference between a bound that can be satisfied by a repair and one that cannot. A floor over total graph edges forbids removing a transitively implied edge, because the total falls; a floor over total-minus-redundant is neutral to that exact repair and still breaches on the removal of a load-bearing edge. Today that distinction requires editing a number by hand, which makes a cleanup byte-indistinguishable from an erosion in the resulting diff. With derived measurements the unit carries the intent, so the enforcement mechanism can tell the two apart without a privileged act. Measurements are addressable by id from every read surface, so an agent composes them with grep and jq, and every measurement reports the cost it incurred to compute."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","assurance","configurability","measurement","query"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":600},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A measurement is created, listed, read, updated and removed through pm commands, persisted as workspace data, and recorded in the immutable history like any other mutation; The source vocabulary covers items, dependency_kind, graph analytics, validate, health, history, links, and extension-contributed providers, and each source declares its own key schema so a declaration naming a removed field fails loudly instead of reading as zero; derived measurements evaluate arithmetic over other measurements, with cycle detection, so denomination is expressible without code; Every evaluation reports its own compute cost and honours an explicit bound on it, so a measurement remains affordable at a million items; Measurement results are addressable in json and toon and stable enough to pipe into jq, with the selector documented in the row contract"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-1jzupz"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":80},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1jzupz","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-7ob5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-96h7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-9gzr4r","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o87av6","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a40c720d58ba5f74579a05fbd9e63e740ff709169cd5089c5bd956fffd1fd36c","message":""}
